WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:01.934
-Welcome back.

00:00:01.934 --> 00:00:04.300
I'm here with Hillary
and Chelsea Clinton.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:07.767
Now, as --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.767 --> 00:00:10.334
We're gonna get to why Hillary
is wearing these headphones.

00:00:10.334 --> 00:00:11.968
As mother and daughter,
I know that you're very close,

00:00:11.968 --> 00:00:13.901
but I want to see
just how close you are

00:00:13.901 --> 00:00:16.033
in a game that we call
"The Mother/Daughter Challenge."

00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:17.968
Here's how the game works.
One of you will wear

00:00:17.968 --> 00:00:19.400
the noise-canceling headphones

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:21.868
while the other answers
a question about you.

00:00:21.868 --> 00:00:23.300
And then,
you'll take off the headphones,

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:24.801
and we'll see
if your answer matches.

00:00:24.801 --> 00:00:26.367
-Okay.
-If it does, you get a point.

00:00:26.367 --> 00:00:28.400
Very good?
-Do we get a prize?

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.634
-Yeah -- What's that?
-Do I get a prize if I win?

00:00:30.634 --> 00:00:31.934
-Uh, yeah, you --
-A suitcase.

00:00:31.934 --> 00:00:33.100
-Yeah, the love of your mother.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:34.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:37.868
-I hope I get that.
I don't know.

00:00:37.868 --> 00:00:39.467
-Now, it's gonna get loud.
-Oh.

00:00:39.467 --> 00:00:40.834
-Ready?
It's gonna get loud.

00:00:40.834 --> 00:00:42.634
Here we go. Hold on.
Tell me whe-- you heard it.

00:00:42.634 --> 00:00:45.300
-Oh, my gosh!
-All right, very good.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:46.634
So you can't hear.
Very good.

00:00:46.634 --> 00:00:48.367
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.367 --> 00:00:50.601
Okay. Ready, Chelsea?
-Okay, I'm ready.

00:00:50.601 --> 00:00:55.033
-What song would your mom sing
at karaoke?

00:00:55.033 --> 00:00:57.634
-I think she only knows
the words to "Moon River."

00:00:57.634 --> 00:00:59.634
[ Laughter ]
I think that's the only song --

00:00:59.634 --> 00:01:02.334
-Is that even at a karaoke?
-I don't know.

00:01:02.334 --> 00:01:04.701
I think it's the only song
she knows the words to.

00:01:04.701 --> 00:01:06.801
The Roots are laughing.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:08.701
-All right, hold on a second.
All right, very good.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.901
All right --
No, take it off.

00:01:10.901 --> 00:01:13.467
-Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh!
-You're getting into the song.

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:15.834
-Whoa!
-All right, the question was,

00:01:15.834 --> 00:01:18.934
what song would you sing
at karaoke?

00:01:18.934 --> 00:01:20.267
-And she answered it?
-Yes.

00:01:20.267 --> 00:01:22.000
-Oh, okay.
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:25.968
Well, probably the only song
she ever heard me sing.

00:01:25.968 --> 00:01:28.167
-Hmm, okay.
-I used to sing to her

00:01:28.167 --> 00:01:29.968
when she was a baby.
-Okay.

00:01:29.968 --> 00:01:32.901
-And I sang the same song.
We would sit in a little chair,

00:01:32.901 --> 00:01:34.701
we'd look out the window,
look at the moon,

00:01:34.701 --> 00:01:35.801
I'd sing "Moon River."

00:01:35.801 --> 00:01:37.300
[ Bell dings ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:39.567
-That's exactly right!

00:01:39.567 --> 00:01:41.067
I love "Moon River."
I love it.

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:42.834
That's a beautiful song.

00:01:42.834 --> 00:01:44.434
Chelsea, it is your turn.
-Okay.

00:01:44.434 --> 00:01:46.701
Oh, gosh, all right.
-It's gonna -- it's loud.

00:01:46.701 --> 00:01:49.067
-It is. It's very loud.
Okay.

00:01:49.067 --> 00:01:50.133
[ Laughter ]
-All right.

00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:51.567
Ooh, you're into it.
Very good.

00:01:51.567 --> 00:01:52.601
You want to give that
to Chelsea?

00:01:52.601 --> 00:01:55.000
-Okay, here you go.
-Okay.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:59.801
Okay. What is your craziest
family-vacation memory?

00:01:59.801 --> 00:02:01.601
-Oh, we -- whew.

00:02:01.601 --> 00:02:03.801
We had a lot of
kind of crazy times.

00:02:03.801 --> 00:02:05.901
I'll tell you -- I hope
she doesn't remember this,

00:02:05.901 --> 00:02:08.367
'cause it was pretty traumatic.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.367 --> 00:02:09.534
-Those are the best stories.

00:02:09.534 --> 00:02:12.133
-We took her to Russia --
Russia --

00:02:12.133 --> 00:02:14.467
When we went on a state visit
when Bill was president.

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:16.467
-Yeah.
-And, you know, there's

00:02:16.467 --> 00:02:20.400
the formal goodbyes, so Bill
and I were ushered into the,

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:23.467
you know, the beast,
the big limousine

00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:25.234
to head to the airport,

00:02:25.234 --> 00:02:28.534
not knowing
that we had left her behind.

00:02:28.534 --> 00:02:29.934
[ Audience "Ohhs" ]

00:02:29.934 --> 00:02:31.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:31.234 --> 00:02:32.267
[ Sad tuba ]
-Wow!

00:02:32.267 --> 00:02:34.367
-I mean, can you imagine...
-Wow!

00:02:34.367 --> 00:02:37.501
-...leaving my only child
in the Kremlin,

00:02:37.501 --> 00:02:40.133
especially with everything
that has happened?

00:02:40.133 --> 00:02:41.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.901 --> 00:02:44.167
-Very good.
Here we go.

00:02:44.167 --> 00:02:45.901
-That was a long answer.
-No, it's a good --

00:02:45.901 --> 00:02:48.667
It's a goodie.
But it doesn't have to be long.

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:51.567
Maybe we added stuff.
-I'm trying to read your lips.

00:02:51.567 --> 00:02:53.968
-No, okay.
-But I didn't succeed at all.

00:02:53.968 --> 00:02:59.868
-My question was, what's the
craziest family vacation memory?

00:02:59.868 --> 00:03:01.300
-Oh, gosh,
now I wish we had been, like,

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:04.334
chased by a bear or something.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.334 --> 00:03:06.934
-Close.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:06.934 --> 00:03:08.801
[ Rimshot ]

00:03:08.801 --> 00:03:09.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:09.901 --> 00:03:12.067
-Craziest...

00:03:16.801 --> 00:03:18.467
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.467 --> 00:03:20.200
I feel like there's
a lot of shock over there.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.868
-No.
No, not shock.

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:24.234
It's fun, it's fun.
-It's fun.

00:03:24.234 --> 00:03:26.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.801 --> 00:03:28.234
When they left me
in the Kremlin.

00:03:28.234 --> 00:03:29.567
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:03:29.567 --> 00:03:30.968
[ Ding! ]

00:03:30.968 --> 00:03:33.100
♪♪

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:35.634
-You remember that?

00:03:35.634 --> 00:03:37.734
Hillary and Chelsea Clinton,
everybody.

00:03:37.734 --> 00:03:40.968
Their new docuseries, "Gutsy,"
will be available on Apple TV+

00:03:40.968 --> 00:03:42.467
starting this Friday.

